From: lazy-cuda-graphs prototype (opportunities/04-lazy-cuda-graphs)
Subject: [PATCH] Lazy CUDA graph capture: capture a traffic-chosen startup set,
 the rest during scheduler idle time

Base: sgl-project/sglang v0.5.20 (94602c9c2b7cbdb8efd5c52802dac6a1c180089e)

Adds opt-in lazy capture to the decode (full) and prefill (breakable) graph
runners. With cuda_graph_config <phase>.initial_bs set, only those buckets are
captured at startup; the remaining planned buckets are captured one per
scheduler iteration while the server is fully idle, in deferred_bs order
(priority-merged across phases), with hot eager buckets promoted. Batches whose
default bucket is not yet captured run eagerly (bucket-exact dispatch, no extra
padding). Steps run in lockstep on all TP ranks: rank 0 proposes a tick through
the existing request broadcast, all ranks agree with one MIN all-reduce on the
CPU group, then capture the same bucket in one graph_capture session.

Default behaviour is unchanged unless initial_bs is given. Unsupported
configurations (speculative decoding, LoRA, PP, DP attention, CP, PD,
torch.compile, memory saver, MLA, hybrid state pools, post-capture KV sizing,
non-default backends) fall back to capture-all with a warning.

Not yet run on a GPU. Unit tests for the two GPU-free modules live outside the
SGLang tree (opportunities/04-lazy-cuda-graphs/tests).

